// COGNITO-SSO-005 — ghost identity with elevated privileges (Soufflé / Datalog).
// Three conditions on a Cognito User Pool create the worst case:
//   1. an external IdP is registered                  pool_has_external_idp(pool, idp)
//   2. no PreSignUp Lambda gate before user creation  pool_missing_presignup(pool)
//   3. a sensitive attribute is mapped from IdP claims sensitive_attribute_mapped(pool, idp, attr, claim)
// Result: an attacker controlling the IdP federates -> ghost identity auto-created
// with the sensitive attribute set from an attacker-controlled claim, no gate.
//
// The finding is per-IdP: it must name the specific IdP with the sensitive
// mapping (the FN trap has one safe IdP and one risky IdP on the same pool).
//
//   souffle ghost_identity.dl -F <facts-dir> -D <out-dir>
//   -> out-dir/ghost_identity.csv lists (pool, idp, attr, claim) — non-empty = FAIL.
//
// Inspired by Doyensec CloudsecTidbits No. 4 — Multi-SSO AWS Cognito User Pools.

.decl pool_has_external_idp(pool:symbol, idp:symbol)
.decl pool_missing_presignup(pool:symbol)
.decl sensitive_attribute_mapped(pool:symbol, idp:symbol, attr:symbol, claim:symbol)
.input pool_has_external_idp
.input pool_missing_presignup
.input sensitive_attribute_mapped

.decl ghost_identity(pool:symbol, idp:symbol, attr:symbol, claim:symbol)
.output ghost_identity
ghost_identity(P, IDP, Attr, Claim) :-
  pool_has_external_idp(P, IDP),
  pool_missing_presignup(P),
  sensitive_attribute_mapped(P, IDP, Attr, Claim).
